   max S_P = 308  (= P*44)
  symmetry of S_P, P=7 (residue-pair invariance test):
     transpose (p,q)->(q,p)  [z->1/z]      : invariant=True   (48 pairs checked)
     neg-p     (p,q)->(-p,q) [z->-z]       : invariant=True   (48 pairs checked)
     neg-q     (p,q)->(p,-q) [z->-z]       : invariant=True   (48 pairs checked)
     modular S (p,q)->(q,-p) [z->-1/z]     : invariant=True   (48 pairs checked)
     double-p  (p,q)->(2p,q) [z->2z]       : invariant=False   (1 pairs checked)
     scale2    (p,q)->(2p,2q)[z->z]        : invariant=False   (1 pairs checked)
     shift     (p,q)->(p+q,q)[z->z+1]      : invariant=False   (1 pairs checked)
     U: (p,q)->(p,p+q)       [z->z/(z+1)]  : invariant=False   (1 pairs checked)
     -- slope-scaling z->c z, c in F_7^* (which c preserve S):
        preserved by c in [1, 6]  (out of 1..6)
  P^1(F_7) slope realization (z = p q^{-1} mod 7; q-residue invertible):
     slope z -> set of S values seen (if not singleton, S is NOT a pure
     function of the slope -> it needs the FULL P^1 quotient, not just z):
        z=   0: S in [0]
        z=   1: S in [84, 224, 308]
        z=   2: S in [140, 168, 252]
        z=   3: S in [140, 168, 252]
        z=   4: S in [140, 168, 252]
        z=   5: S in [140, 168, 252]
        z=   6: S in [84, 224, 308]
        z= inf: S in [0]
  orbits of P^1(F_7) under <z->-z, z->1/z> (Klein 4-grp):
     orbit [0, 'inf']  ->  S [0]
     orbit [1, 6]  ->  S [84, 224, 308]
     orbit [2, 3, 4, 5]  ->  S [140, 168, 252]
  => the quotient P^1(F_7)/<+-,inv> has orbits indexed by the UNORDERED
     pair {||p||,||q||}; that is exactly the symmetry of the f-table.

